  "sourceUrl": "https://docs.fortinet.com/document/fortigate/8.0.2/hardware-acceleration/47902/fortigate-100f-and-101f-fast-path-architecture",
  "notes": "FortiGate 100F/101F fast-path architecture doc: \"Two 10/100/1000BASE-T Copper (DMZ, MGMT). Sixteen 10/100/1000BASE-T Copper (WAN1, WAN2, HA1, HA2, 1 to 12). Two 10 GigE SFP+ (X1 and X2) ... Four 1GigE SFP (13 to 16). Four shared interfaces (17 to 20) that can be either 10/100/1000BASE-T Copper or 1GE SFP.\" Ports 17-20 are therefore modelled as combo pairs: \"there are two sets of physical interfaces numbered 17 to 20 but only one of each can be connected to a network\". Interface names follow FortiOS (port1-port20, wan1/wan2, ha1/ha2, dmz, mgmt, x1/x2) with the SFP half of a shared pair suffixed -sfp because FortiOS gives both halves the same name."
